{/*
  The interactive core-flow diagram — home band 2. The first member of the §5 interactive
  semantic-HTML contract class (docs/design/docs-site-visual-blueprint.md §5): one responsive
  semantic-HTML/CSS representation of the plan-driven spine (seven stages, review loops),
  three independent collapsed-by-default satellite disclosures (gist authoring, objective
  authoring, the docs/learned cache with its harvest + dreaming curation loops), and labeled
  dashed feeds. No <svg> anywhere: all semantics live in source order and visible text;
  connectors are CSS-generated decorative glyphs/rules in the accessibility-neutral
  `content: "…" / ""` form. Colors come only from existing --perk-* / --sl-color-* custom
  properties on §9-verified pairs; every font-size is declared in px and >= 16.

  Layout is container-keyed on the figure's inline size (compositions.css makes
  figure.perk-diagram an inline-size container): vertical spine + stacked satellites by
  default (and in no-container-query browsers), a horizontal wrapping spine from 640px, and a
  three-up satellite row from 960px. No viewport media query.

  No-JS/print strategy: the three <details> ship `open` in source, so the unenhanced page
  (and the static a11y gate, which never runs scripts) is content-complete. The processed
  module script below mounts src/core-flow-controller.mjs, which removes `open` on enhance,
  re-opens on `beforeprint`/restores on `afterprint`, and drives the 9 supplementary tooltips
  (7 stage chips + the 2 cache loops — hover/focus intent, tap pinning on hover-incapable
  devices, a document-level Escape dismiss latch, one visible at a time). Tooltip copy is
  supplementary color only; every tooltip is the sibling of its real <button> trigger inside
  the same position:relative .tip-wrap, with aria-describedby always pointing at it.

  `▸ implement` is shown as an example in-flight stage (visually-hidden `(current)` carries
  the state accessibly); review loops name their shipped surfaces truthfully — human review
  is the universal plan/objective gate, the agent draft-review wave is an optional
  browser-door assist, gist authoring is human-review only.
*/}

<figure class="perk-diagram perk-core-flow" data-core-flow>
  <ol class="flow-spine">
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-plan"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> plan</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-plan" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>A read-only session explores the repo and authors a bounded plan; a human review gates it before save — on the browser review door an agent draft-review wave assists.</span></span>
      <span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human review · optional agent wave</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-save"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> save</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-save" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>The approved plan is persisted as a durable issue — the canonical artifact the rest of the workflow consumes.</span></span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage current">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-implement"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">▸</span> implement<span class="visually-hidden"> (current)</span></button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-implement" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>A worktree session executes the saved plan and runs the repo's CI checks before submitting.</span></span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-submit"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> submit</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-submit" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>The change goes up as a pull request for human review.</span></span>
      <span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human PR review</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage conditional">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-address"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">◇</span> address</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-address" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>Review feedback is classified and resolved — this stage runs only when review asks.</span></span>
      <span class="condition">(if review asks)</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-land"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> land</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-land" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>The approved pull request merges; objective nodes advance and reconcile automatically.</span></span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-learn"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> learn</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-learn" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>Durable learnings from the session are captured into learn issues for later consolidation.</span></span>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="satellites">
    <details open data-core-flow-disclosure>
      <summary><span class="sat-label">gist authoring</span> <span class="sat-hint">problem statements — plan → save</span></summary>
      <div class="sat-body">
        <p class="mini-flow"><span class="mini-stage">plan</span><span class="mini-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="mini-stage">save</span><span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human review</span></p>
        <ul class="feeds">
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> objective plan — seeds an objective</li>
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> spine plan — seeds a plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details open data-core-flow-disclosure>
      <summary><span class="sat-label">objective authoring</span> <span class="sat-hint">plans of plans — plan → save</span></summary>
      <div class="sat-body">
        <p class="mini-flow"><span class="mini-stage">plan</span><span class="mini-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="mini-stage">save</span><span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human review · optional agent wave</span></p>
        <ul class="feeds">
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> spine plan — each node emits a bounded plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details open data-core-flow-disclosure>
      <summary><span class="sat-label">docs/learned</span> <span class="sat-hint">the durable learned-docs cache</span></summary>
      <div class="sat-body">
        <div class="cache">
          <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-harvest"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> harvest → objective authoring</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-harvest" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>Harvest mines docs/learned for improvement opportunities and authors one bounded objective — an objective factory, never a direct plan.</span></span>
          <span class="tip-wrap"><button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-dreaming"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> dreaming — corpus self-curation</button><span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-dreaming" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>Dreaming reads the learned corpus as a whole and authors a reviewed curation objective — pruning and consolidating perk's memory.</span></span>
        </div>
        <ul class="feeds">
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> spine plan — ambient learned context</li>
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> objective plan — ambient learned context</li>
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> gist plan — ambient learned context</li>
          <li class="feed">spine learn <span aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> docs/learned — mediated: /learn captures learn issues; perk learn docs folds them into the corpus</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  /* --- Spine: vertical by default (also the no-container-query rendering) ----------------- */
  .flow-spine {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    row-gap: 6px;
  }

  .stage {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    column-gap: 10px;
    row-gap: 6px;
  }

  /* Decorative CSS-generated connectors (the accessibility-neutral alt form): ↓/→ solid
     transitions, ⇣/⇢ the dashed conditional transition into address. */
  .stage + .stage::before {
    content: "↓" / "";
    inline-size: 100%;
    padding-inline-start: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stage + .stage.conditional::before {
    content: "⇣" / "";
  }

  .stage button[data-core-flow-tip] {
    background: var(--perk-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-control);
    padding: 5px 12px;
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .stage.current button[data-core-flow-tip] {
    border: 2px solid var(--perk-accent);
    padding: 4px 11px;
    color: var(--perk-accent);
  }

  .glyph {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
  }
  .stage.current .glyph {
    color: var(--perk-accent);
  }

  .loop {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .condition {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* --- Satellites: stacked full-width by default ------------------------------------------ */
  .satellites {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-block-start: 24px;
  }

  .satellites details {
    background: var(--perk-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-card);
  }

  .satellites summary {
    padding: 10px 14px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .sat-label {
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .sat-hint {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .sat-body {
    padding: 2px 14px 14px;
  }

  .mini-flow {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    column-gap: 8px;
    row-gap: 6px;
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .mini-stage {
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-control);
    padding: 2px 8px;
  }

  .mini-arrow {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
  }

  /* The docs/learned durable-cache cylinder (CSS-shaped: elliptical rim over a rounded-base
     body; decorative geometry only — the loop labels carry the semantics). */
  .cache {
    position: relative;
    margin-block: 14px 14px;
    padding: 20px 14px 14px;
    background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-block-start: none;
    border-radius: 0 0 50% 50% / 0 0 12px 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    row-gap: 6px;
  }
  .cache::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: -1px;
    inset-block-start: -9px;
    block-size: 18px;
    background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .cache .tip-wrap button {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    text-align: start;
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .feeds {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    row-gap: 6px;
  }

  /* Labeled feeds: the dashed-rule treatment is decoration; the label is the semantics. */
  .feed {
    border-block-start: 1px dashed var(--perk-border);
    padding-block-start: 6px;
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .feed-glyph {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
  }

  /* --- Supplementary tooltips (colocated siblings of their triggers) ---------------------- */
  .tip-wrap {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  [data-core-flow-tooltip] {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: calc(100% + 8px);
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: max-content;
    max-width: min(36ch, calc(100cqw - 16px));
    padding: 8px 10px;
    background: var(--perk-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-control);
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: start;
    z-index: 3;
  }
  [data-core-flow-tooltip][data-align="start"] {
    left: 0;
    transform: none;
  }
  [data-core-flow-tooltip][data-align="end"] {
    left: auto;
    right: 0;
    transform: none;
  }
  [data-core-flow-tooltip][hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* --- Container flips: horizontal spine from 640px, three-up satellites from 960px ------- */
  @container (min-width: 640px) {
    .flow-spine {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      column-gap: 10px;
      row-gap: 14px;
    }
    .stage + .stage::before {
      content: "→" / "";
      inline-size: auto;
      padding-inline-start: 0;
    }
    .stage + .stage.conditional::before {
      content: "⇢" / "";
    }
  }

  @container (min-width: 960px) {
    .satellites {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // The site's first (and only) client script: mount the extracted, unit-tested interaction
  // controller on every core-flow figure. Unenhanced pages (no JS, print, the static a11y
  // gate) are content-complete from source — enhancement only collapses the satellites and
  // adds the supplementary tooltips.
  import { enhanceCoreFlow } from "../core-flow-controller.mjs";

  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll("[data-core-flow]")) {
    enhanceCoreFlow(root);
  }
</script>
